Package: sharedimp
Title: Shared Predictive Importance via Fold-Internal Residualization
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Koki",
           family = "Tsuyuzaki",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "k.t.the-answer@hotmail.co.jp")
Description: A resampling-based implementation of the linear-regression
    variant of ultra-marginal feature importance (UMFI-LR; Janssen, Guan and
    Robeva, 2023, <https://proceedings.mlr.press/v206/janssen23a.html>) for
    modern machine-learning workflows. For each anchor feature, the other
    predictors are residualized on the anchor using coefficients estimated
    inside the training fold only, and the out-of-sample performance of a
    model with the anchor plus residualized predictors is compared, fold by
    fold, with a model using the residualized predictors alone. Importance is
    positive when keeping the anchor predicts better; negative values are not
    truncated. Works with 'parsnip' model specifications, 'rsample'
    resamples and 'yardstick' metrics for regression, binary and multiclass
    classification, with fixed hyperparameters and reproducible random state.
